lly\" and black for \"leave it unchanged\".\n72:    - Left-edge non-corner cells use blue for \"flip this interior row horizontally\" and black for \"leave it unchanged\".\n73:    - Right-edge non-corner cells recolor that interior row's green pixels to the shown non-black color.\n74:    - Bottom-edge non-corner cells recolor that interior column's yellow pixels to the shown non-black color.\n75:    - The interior region contains only black, green, and yellow pixels.\n76:\n77:    Rule:\n78:    - Remove the outer frame conceptually and work on the interior rectangle.\n79:    - First, vertically reverse every interior column whose top instruction cell is red.\n80:    - Second, horizontally reverse every interior row whose left instruction cell is blue.\n81:    - Third, for each row with a non-black right instruction, replace all green pixels in that row with the instruction color.\n82:    - Fourth, for each column with a non-black bottom instruction, replace all yellow pixels in that column with the\n83:      instruction color.\n84:    - Output only the transformed interior rectangle, without the instruction frame.\n85:\n86:    Key insight:\n87:    - Each edge of the frame controls a different operation type, and the flips must happen before recoloring because\n88:      the flips change which rows contain green pixels and which columns contain yellow pixels.\n89:    \"\"\"\n90:    g = np.asarray(grid, dtype=int)\n91:    assert g.ndim == 2\n92:    h, w = g.shape\n93:    assert h >= 3 and w >= 3\n94:\n95:    assert int(g[0, 0]) == BLACK\n96:    assert int(g[0, -1]) == BLACK\n97:    assert int(g[-1, 0]) == BLACK\n98:    assert int(g[-1, -1]) == BLACK\n\n299:def generate_input() -> np.ndarray:\n300:    for _ in range(MAX_GENERATION_ATTEMPTS):\n301:        grid = _gen_attempt()\n302:        if grid is not None:\n303:            return grid\n304:    raise RuntimeError(\"failed to generate a valid instruction-frame puzzle\")\n\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
